71. IMPORTANT SECURITY PRINCIPLE
============================================================

NEVER TRUST THE CLIENT.

Anything coming from:

- browser
- URL
- localStorage
- request body
- query parameter
- WebSocket
- uploaded file
- hidden input
- frontend state

must be treated as untrusted.

The server must independently determine:

identity
permissions
ownership
pricing
availability
roles
business rules
security-sensitive state

